lantern-pr 1
# 41
#title Publish SHA256SUMS with every release
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/41
#branch feat/release-checksums
#base main
#opened 2026-11-12
#head 848f10e6090e3cb4999f2759750988dfa788250b
#describe what Every release now carries a SHA256SUMS file listing the macOS, macOS arm64, Windows and Linux zips, so a download can be checked with sha256sum -c. It needs no key or secret.
#describe before A release had zips and no way to check them.
#describe after The script writes one line per zip; shasum -c prints OK for each, and FAILED for a zip with a changed byte.
#describe verified typecheck, lint and the three workflow tests are green; the script was run on dummy zips.
+ scripts/release-checksums.sh
~ .github/workflows/release.yml
~ README.md
~ docs/installation.md
~ test/release-workflow.test.ts
#order scripts/release-checksums.sh
#order .github/workflows/release.yml
#order test/release-workflow.test.ts
#order README.md
#order docs/installation.md
#reason scripts/release-checksums.sh A script file, because the workflow tests forbid block run steps, writes the checksums in the format sha256sum -c reads.
#reason .github/workflows/release.yml The publish job needs the script and a checkout to run it, so releases carry SHA256SUMS without any secret.
#reason README.md Downloaders need to know how to check a zip against the published checksums.
#reason docs/installation.md The install guide carries the same verify note, with the Linux and macOS commands.
#reason test/release-workflow.test.ts Without a test, moving or deleting the step would ship releases with no checksums or ones missing the arm64 zip.
#story A maintainer publishes a release that can be checked
#step actor Maintainer
#step action publishes
#file .github/workflows/release.yml
#file scripts/release-checksums.sh
#file test/release-workflow.test.ts
#step subject a release
#below actor Release
#below interaction now lists a SHA-256 hash for every zip
#below consequence zips with no way to check => zips with SHA256SUMS
#story A user checks a downloaded zip
#step actor User
#step action checks
#file README.md
#file docs/installation.md
#step subject a downloaded zip
#below actor User
#below interaction sees OK or FAILED for each zip
#below consequence damaged download unnoticed => damaged download shows FAILED
